To add SoundCloud music playback to your website, you'll need to use the **SoundCloud Widget API**. Here's a step-by-step guide:

## 1. Basic Embed Method (Simplest)
### HTML Example:
```html
<!-- Replace TRACK_ID with the actual SoundCloud track ID or URL -->
<iframe width="100%" height="166" 
        scrolling="no" frameborder="no" 
        src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=TRACK_ID&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_credentials=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false">
</iframe>
```

## 2. Using SoundCloud's oEmbed API (Dynamic Embed)
### JavaScript Example:
```html
<div id="soundcloud-player"></div>

<script>
// Replace with your SoundCloud track URL
const trackUrl = "https://soundcloud.com/user/track-name";
const oembedUrl = `https://soundcloud.com/oembed?format=json&url=${encodeURIComponent(trackUrl)}`;

fetch(oembedUrl)
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => {
    const embedHtml = data.html;
    document.getElementById('soundcloud-player').innerHTML = embedHtml;
  })
  .catch(err => console.error('Error:', err));
</script>
```

## 3. Advanced: Using SoundCloud oEmbed API with Controls
### HTML + JavaScript:
```html
<!-- Container for player -->
<div id="player"></div>

<!-- Play/Pause Button -->
<button onclick="togglePlay()">Play/Pause</button>

<script>
let widget;

// Initialize player
function initPlayer(trackUrl) {
    const encodedUrl = encodeURIComponent(trackUrl);
    const apiUrl = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=${encodedUrl}&format=json`;

    fetch(apiUrl)
        .then(response => response.json())
        .then(data => {
            document.getElementById('player').innerHTML = data.html;
            // Wait for iframe to load
            setTimeout(() => {
                const iframe = document.querySelector('#player iframe');
                widget = SC.Widget(iframe);
            }, 1000);
        });
}

// Toggle play/pause
function togglePlay() {
    if (widget) {
        widget.toggle(); // Requires Widget API script
    }
}

// Initialize with a track
initPlayer("https://soundcloud.com/user/track-name");
</script>

<!-- Include SoundCloud Widget API -->
<script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>
```

## 4. Server-Side oEmbed (Recommended for Production)
If you're using a backend (e.g., Node.js/Python), fetch the embed HTML server-side to avoid CORS issues:

### Node.js Example:
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const app = express();

app.get('/embed-soundcloud', async (req, res) => {
    const trackUrl = req.query.url;
    const oembedUrl = `https://soundcloud.com/oembed?format=json&url=${encodeURIComponent(trackUrl)}`;

    try {
        const response = await fetch(oembedUrl);
        const data = await response.json();
        res.send(data.html);
    } catch (error) {
        res.status(500).send('Error fetching SoundCloud embed');
    }
});
```

## Key Notes:
1. **Track URLs**: Use full SoundCloud URLs (e.g., `https://soundcloud.com/user/track-name`).
2. **Widget API**: Include `<script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>` for advanced controls.
3. **API Limits**: No strict rate limits for oEmbed, but avoid excessive calls.
4. **Responsive Design**: Add CSS like `.player-container { width: 100%; }` to make players responsive.

## CSS for Responsiveness:
```css
.player-container {
  position: relative;
  padding-bottom: 56.25%; /* 16:9 Aspect Ratio */
  height: 0;
}

.player-container iframe {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0; left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}
```

