<input type="text" class="form-input" placeholder="Type something...">

<style>
.form-input:focus {
  animation: pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
  border-color: #007bff;
}

@keyframes pulse {
  0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(0, 123, 255, 0.4); }
  70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px rgba(0, 123, 255, 0); }
  100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(0, 123, 255, 0); }
}
</style>
```

Choose the approach that best fits your project. The CSS-only method is lightweight, while the JavaScript version offers more customization. Would you like me to adapt any of these solutions specifically for your form structure?

